<div id="wbViews"><div class="wb-view" data-i="0">
<figure class="browser"><div class="chrome"><span class="cd"></span><span class="cd"></span><span class="cd"></span><span class="url">http://www03.webvan.com/default.asp</span></div><div class="shot live"><div class="ld">Loading the archived page from the Internet Archive…</div><iframe data-src="https://web.archive.org/web/19991127213601if_/http://www03.webvan.com:80/default.asp" title="Archived http://www03.webvan.com/default.asp, Captured Nov 27, 1999 · 21:36 UTC" sandbox="allow-same-origin" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer"></iframe></div></figure>
<figcaption class="wb-cap"><div class="d">Captured Nov 27, 1999 · 21:36 UTC</div><h3>Thanksgiving storefront</h3><p>The Bay Area store five months after launch: a frameset with the cart on the left and a weekly specials column. It promised “Delivery in our vans within the 30-minute window you choose” and “Free delivery and no tipping,” and a banner extended free delivery on all orders through December 31, 1999.</p><div class="warn">Note: Most product images were never archived, so the page renders as layout with empty boxes. Frames are stitched from captures taken on different dates.</div><div class="ex">Peet’s Whole Bean House Blend, 1 lb: $8.97. Land O’ Lakes Butter, 1 lb: $2.47. Lagunitas India Pale Ale, 6-pack: $4.97. Granny Smith apples, large: $0.99 each. “Extended! Free Delivery for All Orders Placed by December 31, 1999.”</div><div class="arch"><a href="https://web.archive.org/web/19991127213601/http://www03.webvan.com:80/default.asp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open this capture on the Wayback Machine ↗</a></div></figcaption>
</div><div class="wb-view" data-i="1" hidden>
